{%- comment -%}
  fye-pdx-ring: the redesigned ring product page (CRO handoff, 27/09/2026).

  Rendered by main-product INSTEAD OF its own markup when the preview gate is
  open (see `pdx` in main-product). Nothing here runs for a visitor while the
  gate is on "preview", so the live page is untouched until Ed flips it.

  Source: Claude Design handoff "Product page CRO redesign", 27/09/2026.
  README plus desktop/mobile screens for plain, engagement, trilogy and
  eternity rings. The prototypes rendered some components twice for mobile;
  this does not (conventions §3). The page grid moves the reassurance tiles
  between columns with grid areas instead.

  ── WHAT IS REUSED, UNCHANGED ─────────────────────────────────────────────

  Every behaviour hangs off the same data-fye-* hooks the old page used, so
  price, cart lines, the picker, the wishlist and ?fyec= links run through
  the one code path in fye-ui.js:

    [data-fye-variants] [data-fye-option] [data-fye-variant-id]
    [data-fye-metal-input] [data-fye-quality] [data-fye-gold-input]
    [data-fye-price] [data-fye-atc] [data-fye-sku] [data-fye-size]
    fye-buybox-centre / -sides / -finish   (with layout: 'pdx')

  The new pieces talk to fye-ui.js through one event, `fye:priced`, which
  render() fires after every repaint. The PDX block at the end of fye-ui.js
  listens and paints the live summary, the carat and shoulder chip prices,
  the "Add to bag · £x" label and the offer saving from it.

  ── WHAT CHANGED FROM THE OLD BUY BOX, AND WHY ────────────────────────────

    · One live price at the top. "Price range" and "Selected price" are gone.
    · Short Title Case name (custom.short_title, else a rule, see below).
      The <title> and meta are untouched: W396 still sets them from the full
      product title.
    · SKU and Categories leave the top; SKU moves into Ring details.
    · Size is never preselected: plain rings used to open on size A.
    · Every ring but a plain band opens on 18ct gold (Ed, 27/09/2026),
      cheapest natural grade within 18ct; W831 alone picked the cheapest
      natural variant in any metal, which was usually palladium.
    · The Diamond Quality select becomes priced chips ("Shoulder diamonds").
    · Nothing is preselected on the centre or side choosers: Ed's 31/08
      "nothing selected" rule, restated 27/09/2026 over the handoff screens
      (which opened on "Choose a diamond" and "Choose a pair", F/G VS).
      Choosing "Choose a diamond" opens the picker at once. The add button
      says what is missing and opens the picker for the centre.
    · The carat stepper becomes "Other versions of this ring".
    · Contact button → Speak to us panel → product enquiry popup.

  ── SHORT TITLE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    custom.short_title, if someone writes one; else
    plain rings: "<profile> Wedding Ring" ("Concave Wedding Ring"); else
    the product title up to its first comma, which drops the carat tail
    ("Claw-Set Full Eternity Ring, 1.55ct total" → "Claw-Set Full Eternity
    Ring"). The carat goes into the summary line instead.

  ── W803 IS HONOURED HERE WITHOUT THE SETTING ─────────────────────────────

  fye-buybox-eternity hides the quality row behind `hide_flat_quality`, a
  setting main-product's schema never declared, so on v3 the hide has never
  actually run. This layout applies the same two-test rule unconditionally,
  because the handoff asks for it. The old page is left as it is.

  Parameters: product, settings, current, crumb_col, is_plain, can_switch,
  profile_slug, width_slug, weight_slug, metal_now, carat_now, colour_now,
  carat_digits, show_centre, show_sides, all computed by main-product.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = settings
  assign p = product
  assign cf = p.metafields.custom
  assign fye = p.metafields.fye
  assign gx = p.metafields.gemex
  assign tags_down = p.tags | join: '~' | downcase | prepend: '~' | append: '~'

  comment
    The breadcrumb's middle step. main-product falls back to the product's
    first collection, which on some rings is the search app's own
    "[XCloud Search app] All products". Skip that and anything like it.
  endcomment
  if crumb_col.handle contains 'cloud-search'
    assign crumb_col = nil
    for c in p.collections
      unless c.handle == 'all' or c.handle contains 'cloud-search'
        assign crumb_col = c
        break
      endunless
    endfor
  endif

  comment
    ── What kind of ring ──
    Tags, not product.type, which is blank on many products (memory:
    shopify-product-type-unreliable). Only one tag is needed for each call.
  endcomment
  assign is_trilogy = false
  if tags_down contains '~trilogy ring~'
    assign is_trilogy = true
  endif
  assign is_full_eternity = false
  if tags_down contains '~full eternity ring~'
    assign is_full_eternity = true
  endif
  assign is_eternity = false
  if tags_down contains '~full eternity ring~' or tags_down contains '~half eternity ring~' or tags_down contains '~eternity~'
    assign is_eternity = true
  endif
  assign is_engagement = false
  if show_centre or tags_down contains '~engagement ring~'
    assign is_engagement = true
  endif

  assign type_word = p.type | default: cf.ring_type.value.first | default: 'Ring'

  comment
    ── Short title ──
  endcomment
  assign short_title = cf.short_title | append: ''
  if short_title == blank
    if is_plain and cf.ring_profile != blank
      assign short_title = cf.ring_profile | append: ' Wedding Ring'
    else
      assign short_title = p.title | split: ',' | first | strip
    endif
  endif

  comment
    ── The summary tail: what the ring IS beyond metal and quality ──
    Plain: width and weight. A centre-stone ring: "1ct round", or on a
    trilogy "0.5ct centre · 1ct total". Otherwise the total diamond weight.
  endcomment
  capture cw_label
    render 'fye-carat-label', value: p.metafields.filters.centre_weight.value
  endcapture
  assign cw_label = cw_label | strip
  capture tdw_label
    render 'fye-carat-label', value: gx.total_diamond_weight
  endcapture
  assign tdw_label = tdw_label | strip

  assign centre_word = fye.centre_shape | append: '' | split: ',' | first | strip | downcase
  if centre_word == blank
    assign centre_word = gx.centre_stone_cut | append: '' | downcase
  endif

  assign tail = ''
  if is_plain
    assign weight_word = cf.ring_weight | append: '' | downcase | capitalize
    assign tail = p.metafields.filters.band_width | append: ''
    if weight_word != blank
      assign tail = tail | append: ' · ' | append: weight_word
    endif
  elsif is_trilogy and cw_label != blank
    assign tail = cw_label | append: 'ct centre'
    if tdw_label != blank
      assign tail = tail | append: ' · ' | append: tdw_label | append: 'ct total'
    endif
  elsif cw_label != blank
    assign tail = cw_label | append: 'ct'
    if centre_word != blank
      assign tail = tail | append: ' ' | append: centre_word
    endif
  elsif tdw_label != blank
    assign tail = tdw_label | append: 'ct total'
  endif

  comment
    ── The metal and quality options (non-plain rings) ──
    Same discovery as fye-buybox-eternity, reading the SAME `current` so the
    highlighted chip and the price describe one ring.
  endcomment
  assign metal_opt = nil
  assign quality_opt = nil
  assign metal_idx = -1
  assign quality_idx = -1
  for option in p.options_with_values
    if option.name == 'Metal'
      assign metal_opt = option
      assign metal_idx = forloop.index0
    elsif option.name contains 'Quality'
      assign quality_opt = option
      assign quality_idx = forloop.index0
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    ── Open on 18ct gold (Ed, 27/09/2026) ──
    Every ring except a plain wedding band opens on 18ct gold, at the
    cheapest NATURAL grade in 18ct: main-product's W831 rule, applied within
    that one metal. The gold colour is the first of the gold swatches
    (Yellow), as before. Left alone when ?variant= chose the ring (shared
    links, back from the bag), and when no 18ct variant is for sale, which
    falls back to W831's pick. Matches "18k Gold" and "18ct Gold" spellings.
  endcomment
  unless is_plain or p.selected_variant or metal_idx < 0
    assign gold18 = nil
    for var in p.variants
      unless var.available
        continue
      endunless
      assign var_metal = var.options[metal_idx] | downcase
      unless var_metal contains '18k' or var_metal contains '18ct'
        continue
      endunless
      assign grade = var.title | split: ' / ' | last | downcase
      if grade contains 'lab'
        continue
      endif
      if gold18 == nil
        assign gold18 = var
      elsif var.price < gold18.price
        assign gold18 = var
      endif
    endfor
    if gold18 != nil
      assign current = gold18
    endif
  endunless

  assign v_metal = ''
  assign v_quality = ''
  if metal_idx >= 0
    assign v_metal = current.options[metal_idx]
  endif
  if quality_idx >= 0
    assign v_quality = current.options[quality_idx]
  endif

  assign v_is_gold = false
  if v_metal contains 'Gold'
    assign v_is_gold = true
  endif

  assign golds = s.gold_colours | default: 'Yellow Gold,White Gold,Rose Gold' | split: ','
  assign gold_default = golds[0] | strip | split: ' ' | first

  comment
    The label the shopper reads: "14ct Yellow Gold", "Platinum". The option
    value itself ("14k Gold") is never changed, label only (W325).
  endcomment
  if is_plain
    assign metal_label = metal_now
  elsif v_is_gold
    assign metal_label = v_metal | replace: 'k Gold', 'ct' | replace: 'K Gold', 'ct' | append: ' ' | append: gold_default | append: ' Gold'
  else
    assign metal_label = v_metal
  endif

  assign preferred_karat = ''
  assign gold_keys = ''
  if metal_opt != nil
    for value in metal_opt.values
      if value contains 'Gold'
        if preferred_karat == blank
          assign preferred_karat = value
        endif
        assign kt = value | downcase | split: 'k' | first | strip
        assign kt_num = kt | plus: 0
        if kt_num > 0
          assign label = kt | append: 'ct'
          assign sort_key = kt
          if kt.size == 1
            assign sort_key = '0' | append: kt
          endif
        else
          assign label = value | remove: ' Gold' | upcase
          assign sort_key = '99'
        endif
        assign entry = sort_key | append: '|' | append: label | append: '|' | append: value
        if gold_keys == blank
          assign gold_keys = entry
        else
          assign gold_keys = gold_keys | append: '~' | append: entry
        endif
      endif
    endfor
  endif
  assign gold_tiles = gold_keys | split: '~' | sort

  comment
    ── W803, unconditionally (see the header) ──
    Two tests must agree: price flat across natural grades within every metal,
    AND tagged `solitaire` + `plain shoulders`, matched whole.
  endcomment
  assign hide_quality = false
  if quality_opt != nil
    if quality_opt.values.size < 2
      assign hide_quality = true
    elsif tags_down contains '~solitaire~' and tags_down contains '~plain shoulders~'
      assign flat = true
      for m in metal_opt.values
        assign first_price = -1
        for var in p.variants
          if var.options[metal_idx] == m
            assign q = var.options[quality_idx] | downcase
            unless q contains 'lab'
              if first_price == -1
                assign first_price = var.price
              elsif var.price != first_price
                assign flat = false
                break
              endif
            endunless
          endif
        endfor
        unless flat
          break
        endunless
      endfor
      if flat
        assign hide_quality = true
      endif
    endif
  endif

  comment
    "Shoulder diamonds" is what the grade means on an engagement ring and a
    trilogy. On an eternity or a set wedding band every stone is graded by
    it, so it keeps its plain name there.
  endcomment
  if is_engagement or is_trilogy
    assign quality_heading = s.pdx_quality_heading | default: 'Shoulder diamonds'
    if show_sides
      assign quality_note = 'The quality of the diamonds set in the shoulders. Your centre diamond and side pair are chosen separately below.'
    elsif show_centre
      assign quality_note = 'The quality of the diamonds set in the shoulders. Your centre diamond is chosen separately below.'
    else
      assign quality_note = 'The quality of the diamonds set in the shoulders.'
    endif
  else
    assign quality_heading = 'Diamond quality'
    assign quality_note = ''
  endif

  comment
    ── Sizes ──
  endcomment
  assign sizes = s.ring_sizes | default: 'A,A.5,B,B.5,C,C.5,D,D.5,E,E.5,F,F.5,G,G.5,H,H.5,I,I.5,J,J.5,K,K.5,L,L.5,M,M.5,N,N.5,O,O.5,P,P.5,Q,Q.5,R,R.5,S,S.5,T,T.5,U,U.5,V,V.5,W,W.5,X,X.5,Y,Y.5,Z,Z.5,Z+1,Z+1.5,Z+2,Z+2.5,Z+3,Z+3.5,Z+4,Z+4.5,Z+5,Z+5.5,Z+6,Z+6.5,Z+7,Z+7.5,Z+8,Z+8.5,Z+9,Z+9.5' | split: ','
  assign threshold = s.surcharge_size | default: 'Q'
  assign size_guide = s.size_guide_url | default: '/pages/find-your-ring-size'
  assign sizer_url = s.pdx_sizer_url | default: '/pages/order-a-free-ring-sizer'

  comment
    ── Lead time, words for the page ──
  endcomment
  assign lead_min = s.pdx_lead_min | default: 10
  assign lead_max = s.pdx_lead_max | default: 14

  comment
    ── Plain ring siblings for "Other versions" ──
    Width and weight are separate PRODUCTS, found by constructing the handle
    exactly as the metal switcher does. all_products allows twenty unique
    handles a page: the metal switcher spends up to seven, this at most four
    widths and two weights.

    Widths come from a setting list; only the two either side of this ring
    are looked up, and a handle that does not exist simply renders no chip.
  endcomment
  assign width_now = p.metafields.filters.band_width | append: '' | remove: 'mm'
  assign width_list = s.pdx_widths | default: '1.5,2,2.5,3,3.5,4,4.5,5,6,7,8,9,10' | remove: ' ' | split: ','
  assign width_at = -1
  for w in width_list
    if w == width_now
      assign width_at = forloop.index0
    endif
  endfor
  assign metal_slug = metal_now | handle
-%}

<section class="band band--white pdx pdx--ring" data-screen-label="Product" data-fye-pdx
         data-noun="{{ s.pdx_noun | default: 'ring' }}"
         data-offer-pct="{{ s.pdx_offer_pct | default: 10 }}">
  <div class="wrap">

    <nav class="pdp__crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a></li>
        {%- if crumb_col -%}
          <li><a href="{{ crumb_col.url }}">{{ crumb_col.title }}</a></li>
        {%- endif -%}
        <li><span aria-current="page">{{ short_title }}</span></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>
    {%- render 'schema-breadcrumbs', mid_name: crumb_col.title, mid_url: crumb_col.url, last_name: p.title, last_url: canonical_url -%}

    <div class="pdx__top">

      {%- comment -%} ---- Gallery ---- {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="pdx__gallery" data-fye-gallery>
        <div class="pdx__stage" data-fye-stage>
          <div class="pdp__wish-over">
            {%- render 'fye-wishlist-button', product: p, context: 'form', size: 'lg' -%}
          </div>

          {%- if p.media.size > 0 -%}
            {%- for media in p.media limit: 8 -%}
              {%- liquid
                if forloop.first
                  assign img_loading = 'eager'
                  assign img_priority = 'high'
                else
                  assign img_loading = 'lazy'
                  assign img_priority = 'auto'
                endif
                assign img_alt = media.alt | default: p.title
              -%}
              <div class="pdp__panel{% if forloop.first %} is-on{% endif %}" data-fye-panel="{{ forloop.index0 }}">
                {{ media | image_url: width: 1400 | image_tag:
                   loading: img_loading,
                   fetchpriority: img_priority,
                   widths: '400,600,900,1200,1400',
                   sizes: '(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 50vw',
                   alt: img_alt,
                   class: 'pdx__img' }}
              </div>
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- else -%}
            <div class="pdp__panel is-on pdx__empty"></div>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if cf.spin_360 != blank -%}
            <div class="pdp__panel pdp__panel--spin" data-fye-panel="spin">
              <div class="Sirv pdx__spin"
                   data-fye-spin
                   data-src="{{ cf.spin_360 }}"
                   data-options="autospin: off; hint.text: Drag to rotate; hint.type: drag;"></div>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            "Shown in 14ct Rose Gold": plain rings only, where the photograph
            IS the metal of this product. A set ring's photograph may be any
            colour, so it would be a claim the image cannot back.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if is_plain and metal_now != blank -%}
            <p class="pdx__tag">Shown in {{ metal_now }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          Real photographs and the 360 only. The handoff's dashed "On hand /
          browse files" tiles were empty design-tool slots, not a feature, and
          are deliberately not built (Ed, 27/09/2026).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if p.media.size > 1 or cf.spin_360 != blank -%}
          <ul class="pdx__thumbs">
            {%- for media in p.media limit: 8 -%}
              <li>
                <button class="pdx__thumb{% if forloop.first %} is-on{% endif %}"
                        type="button"
                        data-fye-thumb="{{ forloop.index0 }}"
                        aria-label="View image {{ forloop.index }}">
                  {{ media | image_url: width: 160 | image_tag:
                     loading: 'lazy',
                     widths: '80,160',
                     sizes: '72px',
                     alt: '' }}
                </button>
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
            {%- if cf.spin_360 != blank -%}
              <li>
                <button class="pdx__thumb pdx__thumb--spin"
                        type="button"
                        data-fye-thumb="spin"
                        aria-label="View in 360 degrees">
                  {{ p.featured_image | image_url: width: 160 | image_tag:
                     loading: 'lazy',
                     widths: '80,160',
                     sizes: '72px',
                     alt: '' }}
                  <span class="pdx__spinbadge" aria-hidden="true">360°</span>
                </button>
              </li>
            {%- endif -%}
          </ul>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        ---- Reassurance ----
        Beside the thumbnails on desktop, after the delivery block on a phone.
        One copy; the page grid moves it (see .pdx__top).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="pdx__assurewrap">
        {%- if is_full_eternity -%}
          {%- render 'fye-pdx-assure', kind: 'full-eternity' -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- render 'fye-pdx-assure', kind: 'ring' -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} ---- Buy box, part one: the decision ---- {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- form 'product', p, class: 'pdx__buy pdx__buy--a', id: 'pdp-form' -%}
        <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ current.id }}" data-fye-variant-id>

        <script type="application/json" data-fye-variants>
          [
            {%- for v in p.variants -%}
              {"id":{{ v.id }},"title":{{ v.title | json }},"price":{{ v.price | json }},"sku":{{ v.sku | json }},"available":{{ v.available }}}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          ]
        </script>

        <div class="pdx__head">
        <p class="pdx__eyebrow">{{ type_word }} · {{ s.pdx_made_line | default: 'Handmade in the UK' }}</p>
        <h1 class="pdx__title" data-fye-product-title>{{ short_title }}</h1>

        <p class="pdx__summary" data-pdx-summary>
          <span data-pdx-sum-metal>{{ metal_label }}</span>
          {%- if quality_opt != nil and hide_quality == false -%}
            <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><span data-pdx-sum-qual>{{ v_quality }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if tail != blank -%}
            <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><span>{{ tail }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </p>

        <p class="pdx__price" data-fye-price aria-live="polite">{{ current.price | money }}</p>
        {%- if show_centre -%}
          <p class="pdx__pricenote">{{ s.pdx_setting_note | default: 'Setting price · Centre diamond not included' }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        <p class="pdx__micro">{{ s.pdx_micro | default: 'VAT included · Handmade to order in the UK · Free insured delivery' }}</p>
        </div>

        <hr class="pdx__rule">

        {%- comment -%} ---- Metal ---- {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if is_plain -%}
          {%- if can_switch -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign colours = 'Yellow Gold,White Gold,Rose Gold,Platinum' | split: ','
              assign carats = '9ct,14ct,18ct' | split: ','
              assign plain_golds = 'Yellow Gold,White Gold,Rose Gold' | split: ','
            -%}
            <div class="pdx__field">
              <p class="pdx__label">Metal <span class="pdx__labelval">{{ metal_now }}</span></p>
              <ul class="pdp__colours">
                {%- for colour in colours -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    assign is_gold = false
                    if plain_golds contains colour
                      assign is_gold = true
                    endif
                    if is_gold
                      assign target_metal = carat_digits | append: 'ct ' | append: colour
                      assign tone = colour | split: ' ' | first | downcase | prepend: '-' | prepend: carat_digits | prepend: '--metal-'
                    else
                      assign target_metal = colour
                      assign tone = '--metal-platinum'
                    endif
                    assign sib_handle = target_metal | handle | append: '-' | append: profile_slug | append: '-wedding-ring-' | append: width_slug | append: '-' | append: weight_slug
                    assign sib = all_products[sib_handle]
                  -%}
                  <li>
                    {%- if colour == colour_now -%}
                      <span class="pdp__colour is-current" style="--sw: var({{ tone }});" aria-current="true">
                        <span class="pdp__dot"></span><span class="pdp__colourname">{{ colour }}</span>
                      </span>
                    {%- elsif sib != blank -%}
                      <a class="pdp__colour" href="{{ sib.url }}" style="--sw: var({{ tone }});">
                        <span class="pdp__dot"></span><span class="pdp__colourname">{{ colour }}</span>
                      </a>
                    {%- else -%}
                      <span class="pdp__colour is-off" style="--sw: var({{ tone }});">
                        <span class="pdp__dot"></span><span class="pdp__colourname">{{ colour }}</span>
                        <span class="visually-hidden">not made in this profile and width</span>
                      </span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </li>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </ul>

              {%- if plain_golds contains colour_now -%}
                <ul class="pdx__carats">
                  {%- for carat in carats -%}
                    {%- liquid
                      assign target_metal = carat | append: ' ' | append: colour_now
                      assign sib_handle = target_metal | handle | append: '-' | append: profile_slug | append: '-wedding-ring-' | append: width_slug | append: '-' | append: weight_slug
                      assign sib = all_products[sib_handle]
                    -%}
                    <li>
                      {%- if carat == carat_now -%}
                        <span class="pdx__ctile is-current" aria-current="true">
                          <span class="pdx__ctilename">{{ carat | upcase }}</span>
                          <span class="pdx__ctileprice" data-pdx-live-price>{{ current.price | money }}</span>
                        </span>
                      {%- elsif sib != blank -%}
                        <a class="pdx__ctile" href="{{ sib.url }}">
                          <span class="pdx__ctilename">{{ carat | upcase }}</span>
                          <span class="pdx__ctileprice">{{ sib.price | money }}</span>
                        </a>
                      {%- else -%}
                        <span class="pdx__ctile is-off">
                          <span class="pdx__ctilename">{{ carat | upcase }}</span>
                          <span class="pdx__ctileprice">Not made</span>
                        </span>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </li>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </ul>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}

        {%- elsif metal_opt != nil -%}
          <div class="pdx__field">
            <p class="pdx__label">Metal <span class="pdx__labelval" data-fye-metal-label>{{ metal_label }}</span></p>

            <ul class="pdp__colours" data-fye-metals data-preferred-karat="{{ preferred_karat | escape }}">
              {%- for colour in golds -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign name = colour | strip
                  assign key = name | split: ' ' | first
                  assign tone = key | downcase | prepend: '--metal-18-'
                -%}
                <li>
                  <button type="button"
                          class="pdp__colour{% if v_is_gold and forloop.first %} is-current{% endif %}"
                          style="--sw: var({{ tone }});"
                          data-fye-gold="{{ key | escape }}">
                    <span class="pdp__dot"></span>
                    <span class="pdp__colourname">{{ name }}</span>
                  </button>
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
              {%- for value in metal_opt.values -%}
                {%- unless value contains 'Gold' -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    if value == 'Platinum'
                      assign tone = '--metal-platinum'
                    else
                      assign tone = '--metal-palladium'
                    endif
                  -%}
                  <li>
                    <button type="button"
                            class="pdp__colour{% if value == v_metal %} is-current{% endif %}"
                            style="--sw: var({{ tone }});"
                            data-fye-metal="{{ value | escape }}">
                      <span class="pdp__dot"></span>
                      <span class="pdp__colourname">{{ value }}</span>
                    </button>
                  </li>
                {%- endunless -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>

            {%- comment -%}
              Carat tiles carry their own price, filled by fye-ui.js from the
              variant for that carat at the current quality. Hidden, not
              absent, on platinum and palladium, so the script can reveal it.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <ul class="pdx__carats" data-fye-karatrow{% unless v_is_gold %} hidden{% endunless %}>
              {%- for tile in gold_tiles -%}
                {%- assign bits = tile | split: '|' -%}
                {%- if bits[2] == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
                <li>
                  <button type="button"
                          class="pdx__ctile{% if bits[2] == v_metal %} is-current{% endif %}"
                          data-fye-metal="{{ bits[2] | escape }}">
                    <span class="pdx__ctilename">{{ bits[1] | upcase }}</span>
                    <span class="pdx__ctileprice" data-pdx-metal-price="{{ bits[2] | escape }}"></span>
                  </button>
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          </div>

          <input type="hidden"
                 name="properties[Gold colour]"
                 value="{{ gold_default | escape }}"
                 data-fye-gold-input
                 {% unless v_is_gold %}disabled{% endunless %}>

          {%- comment -%} MUST precede the quality control: fye-ui.js joins [data-fye-option] in DOM order. {%- endcomment -%}
          <input type="hidden" value="{{ v_metal | escape }}" data-fye-option data-fye-metal-input>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%} ---- Shoulder diamonds / diamond quality ---- {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if quality_opt != nil -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            The value that posts. A hidden input, never a removed control:
            the variant matcher needs one value per option, in order.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <input type="hidden"
                 name="options[{{ quality_opt.name | escape }}]"
                 value="{{ v_quality | escape }}"
                 data-fye-option
                 data-fye-quality>

          {%- unless hide_quality -%}
            <div class="pdx__field" data-pdx-quals>
              <div class="pdx__fieldhead">
                <div class="pdx__labelrow">
                  <p class="pdx__label">{{ quality_heading }} <span class="pdx__labelval" data-pdx-qual-now>{{ v_quality }}</span></p>
                  <a class="pdx__textlink" href="{{ s.quality_help_url | default: '/pages/diamond-4cs' }}">{{ s.pdx_quality_help | default: 'The 4Cs explained' }}</a>
                </div>
                {%- if quality_note != blank -%}
                  <p class="pdx__help">{{ quality_note }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
              <div class="pdx__qgrid" role="radiogroup" aria-label="{{ quality_heading | escape }}">
                {%- for value in quality_opt.values -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    assign vq = value | downcase
                    if vq contains 'lab'
                      assign origin_word = 'Lab-grown'
                    else
                      assign origin_word = 'Natural'
                    endif
                  -%}
                  <button type="button"
                          class="pdx__qtile{% if value == v_quality %} is-on{% endif %}"
                          role="radio"
                          aria-checked="{% if value == v_quality %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
                          data-pdx-qual="{{ value | escape }}">
                    <span class="pdx__qname">{{ value }}</span>
                    <span class="pdx__qorigin">{{ origin_word }}</span>
                    <span class="pdx__qprice" data-pdx-qual-price></span>
                  </button>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>
            </div>
          {%- endunless -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%} ---- The stone choosers, in the new dress ---- {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if show_centre -%}
          {%- render 'fye-buybox-centre', product: p, settings: s, layout: 'pdx' -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if show_sides -%}
          {%- render 'fye-buybox-sides', product: p, settings: s, layout: 'pdx' -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          ---- Ring size ----
          NEVER PRESELECTED. Plain rings: the size IS the variant option, so
          the select carries data-fye-option; until it is chosen fye-ui.js
          prices the page off the opening variant, and the browser's own
          `required` check stops the form posting without one. Every other
          ring: a line-item property, with the oversize surcharge flag.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="pdx__field">
          <div class="pdx__labelrow">
            <label class="pdx__label" for="pdx-size">Ring size</label>
            <a class="pdx__textlink" href="{{ size_guide }}">{{ s.pdx_size_guide_label | default: 'Size guide' }}</a>
          </div>

          {%- if is_plain -%}
            {%- assign size_option = nil -%}
            {%- for option in p.options_with_values -%}
              {%- if option.name contains 'Size' -%}{%- assign size_option = option -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
            {%- if size_option != nil -%}
              <select class="pdx__select" id="pdx-size" name="options[{{ size_option.name | escape }}]" data-fye-option required>
                <option value="">{{ s.pdx_size_placeholder | default: 'Select your UK size' }}</option>
                {%- for value in size_option.values -%}
                  <option value="{{ value | escape }}"{% if p.selected_variant and current.title == value %} selected{% endif %}>{{ value }}</option>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </select>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- else -%}
            <select class="pdx__select"
                    id="pdx-size"
                    name="properties[Ring size]"
                    data-fye-size
                    data-threshold="{{ threshold }}"
                    required>
              <option value="">{{ s.pdx_size_placeholder | default: 'Select your UK size' }}</option>
              {%- for size in sizes -%}
                <option>{{ size | strip }}</option>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </select>
            <input type="hidden" name="properties[_size_surcharge]" value="Yes" data-fye-surcharge disabled>
            <p class="pdx__help" data-fye-surcharge-note hidden>
              {{ s.surcharge_note | default: 'Sizes above Q use more metal, so a 10% surcharge applies. It is shown in the cart.' }}
            </p>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if is_full_eternity -%}
            <div class="pdx__sizebox pdx__sizebox--careful">
              {%- render 'icon', name: 'info', size: 20 -%}
              <div>
                <p class="pdx__sizeboxtitle">Please choose your size carefully</p>
                <p>Full eternity rings cannot be resized because stones are set around the entire band. If you're unsure of your size, order a free ring sizer before placing your order.</p>
                <a class="pdx__caps" href="{{ sizer_url }}">Order a free ring sizer</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          {%- else -%}
            <div class="pdx__sizebox">
              <p>Not sure of your size? We'll send you a <strong>free ring sizer</strong>. Every ring also includes one complimentary resize within the first year.</p>
              <a class="pdx__caps" href="{{ sizer_url }}">Order sizer</a>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- comment -%} ---- Finish, plain rings only ---- {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if is_plain -%}
          {%- render 'fye-buybox-finish', product: p, settings: s, layout: 'pdx' -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          ---- Engraving ----
          The same fee line and the same disabled-when-off inputs as before.
          The checkbox row is a button with data-fye-engrave-set="toggle",
          which fye-ui.js flips between yes and no through the one handler.
          The font is a hidden input the tiles write to; a set of radios would
          all be read by ringProps(), which only skips unticked CHECKBOXES.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if s.engraving and s.engraving_variant_id != blank -%}
          {%- assign font_list = s.engraving_fonts | default: 'Classic Script|Elegant Serif|Modern Sans|Block Capitals' | split: '|' -%}
          <div class="pdx__engrave"
               data-fye-engrave
               data-fee-variant="{{ s.engraving_variant_id }}"
               data-fee-price="{{ s.engraving_price_pennies | default: 5500 }}">
            <button type="button" class="pdx__check" role="checkbox" aria-checked="false" data-fye-engrave-set="toggle">
              <span class="pdx__box" aria-hidden="true">{%- render 'icon', name: 'check', size: 14 -%}</span>
              <span class="pdx__checklabel">{{ s.pdx_engrave_label | default: 'Add a personal engraving inside the band' }}</span>
              <span class="pdx__checkprice">{{ s.engraving_price_label | default: '+£55' }}</span>
            </button>

            <div class="pdx__engravebody" data-fye-engrave-body hidden>
              <div class="pdx__engraverow">
                <label class="visually-hidden" for="pdx-engrave-text">Your engraving</label>
                <input class="pdx__input"
                       id="pdx-engrave-text"
                       type="text"
                       name="properties[Engraving]"
                       data-fye-engrave-text
                       maxlength="{{ s.engraving_max | default: 35 }}"
                       placeholder="{{ s.engraving_placeholder | default: 'Engraving (35 characters max)' | escape }}"
                       disabled>
                <span class="pdx__count" data-fye-engrave-count>0/{{ s.engraving_max | default: 35 }}</span>
              </div>

              <input type="hidden" name="properties[Engraving font]" value="{{ font_list[1] | default: font_list[0] | strip | escape }}" data-fye-engrave-font data-pdx-font-input disabled>
              <div class="pdx__fonts" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Engraving font">
                {%- for f in font_list -%}
                  {%- assign fname = f | strip -%}
                  {%- assign fkey = fname | handle -%}
                  <button type="button"
                          class="pdx__font pdx__font--{{ fkey }}{% if forloop.index == 2 %} is-on{% endif %}"
                          role="radio"
                          aria-checked="{% if forloop.index == 2 %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
                          data-pdx-font="{{ fname | escape }}">
                    <span class="pdx__fontsample" data-pdx-font-sample>{{ s.pdx_engrave_sample | default: 'Always & forever' }}</span>
                    <span class="pdx__fontname">{{ fname }}</span>
                  </button>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          ---- Other versions of this ring ----
          Plain rings: width and weight siblings, by handle. Everything else:
          the design family (fye.family), labelled by fye.family_carat, the
          same data the old carat stepper used. A row with no siblings is not
          drawn, and the block disappears if no row is.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- capture versions_rows -%}
          {%- if is_plain and can_switch -%}
            {%- if width_at >= 0 -%}
              {%- capture width_chips -%}
                {%- assign w_from = width_at | minus: 2 -%}
                {%- assign w_to = width_at | plus: 2 -%}
                {%- for w in width_list -%}
                  {%- assign wi = forloop.index0 -%}
                  {%- if wi < w_from or wi > w_to -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
                  {%- if wi == width_at -%}
                    <span class="pdx__vchip is-current" aria-current="true">{{ w }}mm</span>
                  {%- else -%}
                    {%- assign w_slug = w | remove: '.' | append: 'mm' -%}
                    {%- assign sib_handle = metal_slug | append: '-' | append: profile_slug | append: '-wedding-ring-' | append: w_slug | append: '-' | append: weight_slug -%}
                    {%- assign sib = all_products[sib_handle] -%}
                    {%- if sib != blank -%}
                      <a class="pdx__vchip" href="{{ sib.url }}">{{ w }}mm</a>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
              {%- endcapture -%}
              {%- if width_chips contains '<a ' -%}
                <div class="pdx__vrow"><span class="pdx__vlabel">Width</span><div class="pdx__vchips">{{ width_chips }}</div></div>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- capture weight_chips -%}
              {%- assign weights = 'light|Light,medium|Medium,heavy|Heavy' | split: ',' -%}
              {%- for wt in weights -%}
                {%- assign wbits = wt | split: '|' -%}
                {%- if wbits[0] == weight_slug -%}
                  <span class="pdx__vchip is-current" aria-current="true">{{ wbits[1] }}</span>
                {%- else -%}
                  {%- assign sib_handle = metal_slug | append: '-' | append: profile_slug | append: '-wedding-ring-' | append: width_slug | append: '-' | append: wbits[0] -%}
                  {%- assign sib = all_products[sib_handle] -%}
                  {%- if sib != blank -%}
                    <a class="pdx__vchip" href="{{ sib.url }}">{{ wbits[1] }}</a>
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endcapture -%}
            {%- if weight_chips contains '<a ' -%}
              <div class="pdx__vrow"><span class="pdx__vlabel">Weight</span><div class="pdx__vchips">{{ weight_chips }}</div></div>
            {%- endif -%}

          {%- else -%}
            {%- assign fam = fye.family.value -%}
            {%- if fam != blank and fam.size > 1 -%}
              {%- if s.carat_scale == 'Diamond weight' -%}
                {%- assign fam_label = 'Weight' -%}
              {%- else -%}
                {%- assign fam_label = 'Centre' -%}
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- capture fam_chips -%}
                {%- assign seen = '~' -%}
                {%- for m in fam limit: 8 -%}
                  {%- if m == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
                  {%- comment -%}
                    family_carat is a LIST (list.number_decimal) on the live
                    store, so its first entry is the weight. A single number
                    has no .first and falls through to itself.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  {%- assign m_fc = m.metafields.fye.family_carat.value.first | default: m.metafields.fye.family_carat.value -%}
                  {%- capture m_ct -%}{%- render 'fye-carat-label', value: m_fc -%}{%- endcapture -%}
                  {%- assign m_ct = m_ct | strip -%}
                  {%- if m.handle == p.handle -%}
                    <span class="pdx__vchip is-current" aria-current="true">{% if m_ct != blank %}{{ m_ct }}ct{% else %}This ring{% endif %}</span>
                  {%- else -%}
                    {%- if m_ct == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
                    {%- assign key = '~' | append: m_ct | append: '~' -%}
                    {%- if seen contains key -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
                    {%- assign seen = seen | append: m_ct | append: '~' -%}
                    <a class="pdx__vchip" href="{{ m.url }}">{{ m_ct }}ct</a>
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
              {%- endcapture -%}
              {%- if fam_chips contains '<a ' -%}
                <div class="pdx__vrow"><span class="pdx__vlabel">{{ fam_label }}</span><div class="pdx__vchips">{{ fam_chips }}</div></div>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endcapture -%}

        {%- if versions_rows contains 'pdx__vrow' -%}
          <nav class="pdx__versions" aria-label="{{ s.pdx_versions_label | default: 'Other versions of this ring' | escape }}">
            <p class="pdx__vhead">{{ s.pdx_versions_label | default: 'Other versions of this ring' }}</p>
            {{ versions_rows }}
          </nav>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          ---- The button ----
          Its words come from fye-ui.js: "Choose centre diamond" while a
          stone is outstanding, otherwise "Add to bag · £total". The markup
          holds the plain label because render() remembers it as the default.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="pdx__buyfoot">
        <button class="btn btn--block pdx__atc" type="submit" name="add" data-fye-atc{% unless current.available %} disabled{% endunless %}>
          {%- if current.available -%}
            {{ s.atc_label | default: 'Add to bag' }}
          {%- else -%}
            {{ s.mto_label | default: 'Made to order, enquire' }}
          {%- endif -%}
        </button>

        {%- liquid
          if is_full_eternity
            assign deliv_sub = 'Free insured UK delivery · Free ring sizer before you order'
          else
            assign deliv_sub = 'Free insured UK delivery · Free first resize within 12 months'
          endif
        -%}
        {%- render 'fye-pdx-delivery', lead_min: lead_min, lead_max: lead_max, sub: deliv_sub -%}
        </div>
      {%- endform -%}

      {%- comment -%} ---- Buy box, part two: reassurance and reference ---- {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="pdx__buy pdx__buy--b">
        {%- render 'fye-pdx-engage', product: p, settings: s, context: 'form', noun: 'ring', offer: 'ring', is_plain: is_plain, is_engagement: is_engagement -%}

        <div class="pdx__accs">
          <details class="pdx__acc" open>
            <summary class="pdx__accsum">{{ s.pdx_details_heading | default: 'Ring details' }}</summary>
            <div class="pdx__accbody">
              {%- if p.description != blank -%}
                <div class="pdx__story rte">{{ p.description }}</div>
              {%- endif -%}
              <dl class="pdx__specs">
                {%- if is_plain -%}
                  {%- if metal_now != blank -%}<div><dt>Metal</dt><dd>{{ metal_now }}</dd></div>{%- endif -%}
                  {%- if cf.ring_profile != blank -%}<div><dt>Profile</dt><dd>{{ cf.ring_profile }}</dd></div>{%- endif -%}
                  {%- if p.metafields.filters.band_width != blank -%}<div><dt>Width</dt><dd>{{ p.metafields.filters.band_width }}</dd></div>{%- endif -%}
                  {%- if cf.ring_weight != blank -%}<div><dt>Weight</dt><dd>{{ cf.ring_weight }}</dd></div>{%- endif -%}
                  {%- if size_option != nil and size_option.values.size > 1 -%}
                    <div><dt>Sizes</dt><dd>UK {{ size_option.values.first }} to {{ size_option.values.last }}</dd></div>
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- else -%}
                  {%- if gx.style != blank -%}<div><dt>Style</dt><dd>{{ gx.style }}</dd></div>{%- endif -%}
                  {%- if gx.setting != blank -%}<div><dt>Setting</dt><dd>{{ gx.setting }}</dd></div>{%- endif -%}
                  {%- if gx.centre_stone_cut != blank -%}
                    <div><dt>Centre stone</dt><dd>{{ gx.centre_stone_cut }}{% if cw_label != blank %}, {{ cw_label }}ct{% endif %}</dd></div>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  {%- if tdw_label != blank -%}<div><dt>Total diamonds</dt><dd>{{ tdw_label }}ct</dd></div>{%- endif -%}
                  {%- if metal_opt != nil -%}<div><dt>Metal</dt><dd data-pdx-sum-metal>{{ metal_label }}</dd></div>{%- endif -%}
                  {%- if quality_opt != nil and hide_quality == false -%}<div><dt>{{ quality_heading }}</dt><dd data-pdx-sum-qual>{{ v_quality }}</dd></div>{%- endif -%}
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if current.sku != blank -%}<div><dt>SKU</dt><dd data-fye-sku>{{ current.sku }}</dd></div>{%- endif -%}
              </dl>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="pdx__acc">
            <summary class="pdx__accsum">Delivery &amp; returns</summary>
            <div class="pdx__accbody">{{ s.pdx_acc_delivery | default: '<p>Each ring is handmade to order in the UK and delivered free, fully insured.</p>' }}</div>
          </details>

          <details class="pdx__acc">
            {%- if is_full_eternity -%}
              <summary class="pdx__accsum">Sizing</summary>
              <div class="pdx__accbody">{{ s.pdx_acc_sizing_full | default: '<p>Full eternity rings cannot be resized, because stones are set around the entire band. Please confirm your size with a free ring sizer before ordering.</p>' }}</div>
            {%- else -%}
              <summary class="pdx__accsum">Sizing &amp; resizing</summary>
              <div class="pdx__accbody">{{ s.pdx_acc_sizing | default: '<p>Order a free ring sizer if you are unsure. Every ring includes a complimentary resize within the first year.</p>' }}</div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </details>

          <details class="pdx__acc">
            <summary class="pdx__accsum">Hallmarking &amp; ethics</summary>
            <div class="pdx__accbody">{{ s.pdx_acc_ethics | default: '<p>Every ring is independently hallmarked and supplied with a certificate of authenticity. Ethically sourced, independently certified, fairly priced.</p>' }}</div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- render 'fye-pdx-enquire', product: p, noun: 'ring', price: current.price -%}
</section>
